<body>
<header class="top wrap">
  <p class="eyebrow">Record review · July 31 to October 29, 2026 · Prepared November 2, 2026</p>
  <h1>Ownership Questions Across the DRI Team</h1>
  <p class="lede">How written questions about ownership, authority and sign-off from the nine DRIs were answered over 90 days, measured against factual questions and against other participants.</p>
</header>

<nav class="steps" aria-label="Sections">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="steps-inner" id="steps"></div>
  </div>
  <div class="progress"><span id="bar"></span></div>
</nav>

<main class="wrap">
  <div class="toolbar"><button class="linkbtn" id="toggleAll" type="button">Show all sections on one page</button></div>

  <!-- 0 -->
  <section class="panel" id="overview" data-title="At a glance">
    <p class="kicker">Overview</p>
    <h2>At a glance</h2>
    <p class="sub">Select a figure to open the section it comes from. Use the arrow keys or the buttons at the bottom of each section to move through the review.</p>
    <div class="grid g4" id="stats"></div>
  </section>

  <!-- 1 -->
  <section class="panel" id="scope" data-title="Scope and method">
    <p class="kicker">Section 1</p>
    <h2>Scope and method</h2>
    <p class="sub">What was reviewed, and how each question was coded.</p>
    <div class="card">
      <ul class="clean">
        <li><b>Period.</b> July 31 to October 29, 2026 (90 days).</li>
        <li><b>Sources.</b> 25 Slack channels (19 state-client, 6 cross-team), with asks found in 24. In the cross-team channels, only asks made by or to DRIs were coded. Linear issues, email and meeting notes were consulted for individual threads. Direct messages and huddles were not reviewed.</li>
        <li><b>Population.</b> The nine DRIs on the DRI team roster, labeled DRI A to DRI I. The DRI manager is not in the population.</li>
        <li><b>Unit.</b> An ask is a written request for an answer or an action. Each ask was classed as <i>ownership</i> (who decides, who owns, sign-off, permission, commitment, assignment) or <i>factual</i> (information, logistics).</li>
        <li><b>Outcome.</b> Each ask was coded resolved, partial, redirected, acknowledged only, or no visible response. Resolved means the record shows the answer or action requested.</li>
        <li><b>Totals.</b> 318 asks by DRIs (187 ownership, 131 factual). 263 asks by other participants (126 ownership, 137 factual) serve as a reference group.</li>
        <li><b>Statistics.</b> Wilson 95% intervals; one-sided Fisher exact tests; permutation tests stratified by channel or by phase, 20,000 draws each.</li>
        <li><b>Review.</b> 91 threads addressed to engineering were re-read in a second pass, which changed six outcome codes. Figures use the corrected codes.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 2 -->
  <section class="panel" id="resolution" data-title="Ownership vs factual">
    <p class="kicker">Section 2</p>
    <h2>Ownership questions resolve less often than factual questions</h2>
    <p class="sub">Across the nine DRIs, 58% of ownership questions were resolved (109 of 187), against 76% of factual questions (100 of 131). Ownership questions from other participants were resolved 73% of the time (92 of 126). The median first reply came after 0.83 hours for ownership questions and 0.2 hours for factual ones.</p>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>What happened to each question</h3>
      <p class="note" style="margin:0 0 12px">Hover or tap a segment for counts.</p>
      <svg class="chart" id="mix" viewBox="0 0 760 150" role="img" aria-label="Outcome of DRI ownership and factual questions"></svg>
      <div class="legend" id="mixLegend"></div>
      <p class="note">Of the 78 unresolved ownership questions, 32 received no visible response, 23 were acknowledged only, 18 received a partial answer and 5 were redirected.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Ownership-question resolution varied widely across the nine DRIs</h3>
      <p class="note" style="margin:0 0 8px">Dots: share resolved. Bars: 95% Wilson interval. Dashed line: all nine DRIs. Dotted line: other participants.</p>
      <svg class="chart" id="forest" role="img" aria-label="Ownership questions resolved, by DRI"></svg>
      <details class="data"><summary>View as a table</summary><div class="tablewrap"><table id="forestTable"></table></div></details>
    </div>
    <p>The spread for factual questions was narrower: 67% to 89% among DRIs with at least five factual asks. DRI I's ownership rate rests on four asks. DRI H's interval does not overlap DRI A's; the intervals of DRIs B to G overlap one another.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- 3 -->
  <section class="panel" id="addressees" data-title="Where questions go">
    <p class="kicker">Section 3</p>
    <h2>Where ownership questions go</h2>
    <p class="sub">Half of DRI ownership questions (91 of 187) named an engineer as the first recipient.</p>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Ownership questions by first-named recipient</h3>
      <p class="note" style="margin:0 0 8px">Band width is the number of questions. Select a recipient to see its outcomes.</p>
      <svg class="chart" id="flow" role="img" aria-label="DRI ownership questions by addressee role"></svg>
      <div class="detail" id="flowDetail" aria-live="polite"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Engineering-addressed questions, re-read in full (n=91)</h3>
      <div class="tablewrap"><table>
        <thead><tr><th>Measure</th><th class="num">Share</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Named engineer responded</td><td class="num">67%</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Response named an owner or a commitment</td><td class="num">62%</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Resolved</td><td class="num">59%</td></tr>
          <tr><td>No visible response</td><td class="num">20%</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Redirected, or work returned to the asker</td><td class="num">10%</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Re-raised to the DRI manager or leadership within seven days</td><td class="num">7%</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>
      <p class="note">The median first substantive response came after 0.6 hours.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>What was being asked of engineering</h3>
      <p class="note" style="margin:0 0 12px">41 of the 91 (45%) asked an engineer for a decision, a permission, or a review of non-code work (dates, documents, scope, whether an action was allowed), not for engineering work.</p>
      <svg class="chart" id="kind" viewBox="0 0 760 130" role="img" aria-label="Resolution of engineering-addressed questions by kind of request"></svg>
    </div>
    <p>Questions addressed to a group or a channel, with no named recipient, had the lowest resolution of any addressee type.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- 4 -->
  <section class="panel" id="phase" data-title="Project phase">
    <p class="kicker">Section 4</p>
    <h2>Project phase</h2>
    <p class="sub">States were classed by phase during the period. Two states that started in or near July, and one state in the month before its September launch, are early. All other active states are live. One dormant state and the six cross-team channels are excluded.</p>
    <div class="card">
      <div class="seg" role="group" aria-label="Population">
        <button type="button" data-ph="all" aria-pressed="true">All DRIs</button>
        <button type="button" data-ph="exH" aria-pressed="false">Excluding DRI H</button>
        <button type="button" data-ph="H" aria-pressed="false">DRI H against the rest</button>
      </div>
      <svg class="chart" id="phaseChart" viewBox="0 0 760 220" role="img" aria-label="Ownership questions resolved by project phase"></svg>
      <div class="detail" id="phaseDetail" aria-live="polite"></div>
    </div>
    <ul class="clean">
      <li>16 of the 25 early-phase questions came from one DRI (DRI H).</li>
      <li>The only DRI assigned to a newly started state with no prior engagement (DRI I) resolved 1 of 4.</li>
      <li>With askers shuffled within each phase, DRI H's difference from the other DRIs holds (one-sided p = 0.007, 20,000 draws).</li>
      <li>Because one DRI holds most early-phase questions, phase and individual cannot be fully separated in this sample.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <!-- 5 -->
  <section class="panel" id="rights" data-title="Decision rights">
    <p class="kicker">Section 5</p>
    <h2>Decision rights in the written record</h2>
    <p class="sub">No single written list of the portal settings a DRI may change in production, with or without approval, was found in the reviewed sources. Statements of DRI authority appear as individual channel posts. Select an entry to read the record.</p>
    <div class="card"><ol class="tl" id="timeline"></ol></div>
    <ol class="obs">
      <li>The authority statement that applied on Oct 28 had been posted 89 days earlier. None of the Oct 28 responses referred to it.</li>
      <li>The same DRI acted without prior confirmation twice. The action on an engineering-owned field (issue status) was corrected. The action on a portal node setting was endorsed.</li>
      <li>When a named engineer was asked directly for a specific permission, the answer came within one minute. When the question was who holds a permission, no owner was named.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <!-- 6 -->
  <section class="panel" id="depended" data-title="What resolution depended on">
    <p class="kicker">Section 6</p>
    <h2>What resolution depended on</h2>
    <p class="sub">Five conditions in the record that went with a question being resolved or not.</p>
    <div class="grid g2">
      <div class="card"><h3>A response is not a resolution</h3>
        <p>Of the 78 unresolved DRI ownership questions, 46 (59%) received some reply: an acknowledgment, a partial answer, or a redirect.</p>
        <p style="margin-bottom:0">In engineering-addressed threads, the named engineer replied to DRI H at the same rate as to the other DRIs (67% each) and sooner (median 0.37 hours against 0.69). The replies to DRI H ended in a resolution less often: 33% against 64%.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><h3>A named recipient</h3>
        <svg class="chart" id="named" viewBox="0 0 360 130" role="img" aria-label="Resolution by named recipient versus group or channel"></svg>
        <p class="note">Named person: 104 of 174. Group or channel: 5 of 13.</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Who asked</h3>
      <p class="note" style="margin:0 0 12px">The same question, in one state, on Oct 29.</p>
      <div class="pair">
        <div class="side"><div class="who">A DRI asks the embedded engineer</div><div class="t">4:06 PM</div><div class="res">How was a prior deliverable produced? <br><b>Redirected.</b></div></div>
        <div class="side"><div class="who">The DRI manager asks, after the DRI raised it in a live discussion</div><div class="t">6:44 PM</div><div class="res">Same question, in writing. <br><b>Direct answer in 55 minutes.</b></div></div>
      </div>
      <p class="note">A single matched pair: the asker's rank, the timing and the wording all differ.</p></div>
    <div class="grid g2">
      <div class="card"><h3>How work was returned</h3>
        <p style="margin-bottom:0">In 9 of the 91 engineering-addressed threads, the work was redirected or returned to the asker. In one case, the return came with a five-step written guide and an offer to walk through it. In another, on Oct 29, the return ("you'd need to do the writing") came with no instructions.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><h3>Escalation</h3>
        <p style="margin-bottom:0">6 of the 91 engineering-addressed questions (7%) were re-raised to the DRI manager or leadership within seven days. Ownership questions addressed to the DRI manager directly were resolved 52% of the time (11 of 21).</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 7 -->
  <section class="panel" id="unowned" data-title="No owner of record">
    <p class="kicker">Section 7</p>
    <h2>Items with no owner of record, as of November 1</h2>
    <p class="sub">Five ownership questions raised in writing on Oct 28 and Oct 29 have no named owner or recorded decision in Slack, email, Linear or meeting notes. Select an item for the record.</p>
    <div class="items" id="items"></div>
  </section>

  <!-- 8 -->
  <section class="panel" id="limits" data-title="Limits">
    <p class="kicker">Section 8</p>
    <h2>Limits of the evidence</h2>
    <p class="sub">What this review can and cannot show.</p>
    <div class="card"><ul class="clean">
      <li><b>Written record only.</b> Direct messages, huddles and calls were not reviewed. A question resolved in those places appears here as unresolved.</li>
      <li><b>Coding.</b> Asks were coded by one reviewer with AI assistance. No second independent coder was used, and agreement between coders was not measured. The ownership and factual classes, and the split between decision requests and engineering work, involve judgment.</li>
      <li><b>Sample size.</b> Several DRIs have fewer than 15 ownership questions, and one has 4. Individual intervals are wide.</li>
      <li><b>Phase.</b> Most early-phase questions come from one DRI, so the effect of phase cannot be separated from the effect of the individual.</li>
      <li><b>Addressee.</b> Each question is assigned to its first-named recipient. Questions with several recipients are counted once.</li>
      <li><b>Cause.</b> The record shows sequence and content. It does not show intent or cause.</li>
      <li><b>Attributes.</b> No personal attributes of the DRIs were recorded or analyzed.</li>
      <li><b>Origin.</b> This review was initiated by one of the nine DRIs in the population.</li>
    </ul></div>
  </section>
</main>

<footer><div class="wrap">Source: coded Slack asks, July 31 to October 29, 2026, with Linear, email and meeting notes for individual threads. DRIs are labeled A to I in order of ownership-question resolution.</div></footer>
